# Shell scripts must stay LF even on Windows checkouts (core.autocrlf
# would otherwise turn them CRLF, which breaks strict bash on WSL/Linux
# — see docs/test-plan-read-tool.md §执行环境).
*.sh text eol=lf
# go:embed serves the WORKING-TREE bytes, and the W1.5 hash test pins
# them (webPageSHA256 in webfrontend_static_test.go). A Windows
# core.autocrlf checkout rewrites LF→CRLF on disk, the embedded page
# drifts (nightly 2026-11-18: got f3415179… vs want b4323190…), and the
# pin fails. Embedded assets must be byte-identical on every platform —
# same rationale as the *.sh rule above.
internal/controlplane/webfrontend.html text eol=lf
